      "writtenOn": "2024-03-21T13:00:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, project and caller should become parameters on the experiment REST endpoints (planned as follow-up change).\n\nE.g.:\n\n```\nGET /config/server/experiments/?project\u003dfoo\u0026caller\u003dbar\n\n{\n  \"GerritBackendFeature__allow_fix_suggestions_in_comments\": {\n    \"enabled\": false\n  },\n  \"GerritBackendFeature__attach_nonce_to_documentation\": {\n    \"enabled\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `enabled` flag then reflects whether the experiment is enabled for the project and user that were provided on the request.\n\nThe environment is probably already implicit, depending on whether you call this endpoint in prod, canary or staging, isn\u0027t it?\n\nDoes this make sense?",
